      "seed": 2016128500,
      "version": 460,
      "versionNonce": 806969716,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783254691890,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Call Stack (CS)\n\nCall Stack ek **LIFO (Last In, First Out)** data structure hai.\n\nIsme JavaScript Engine **Execution Contexts** ko push aur pop karta hai.\n\n### Kaam\n\n* Jab program start hota hai, **Global Execution Context** stack me push hota hai.\n* Jab koi function call hota hai, uska **Function Execution Context** stack ke top par push hota hai.\n* Function ka execution complete hone ke baad uska Execution Context stack se pop (destroy) ho jata hai.\n* Is process se JavaScript ko pata chalta hai ki kaunsa code pehle execute hoga aur kaunsa baad me.\n\n### Call Stack ko manager kyu bolte hain?\n\nCall Stack decide karta hai:\n\n* Kaunsa function abhi execute hoga.\n* Kaunsa function wait karega.\n* Execution complete hone par kaunsa context remove hoga.\n* Control kis context ko wapas dena hai.\n\n### Agar Call Stack na ho\n\nJavaScript Engine ko ye pata hi nahi chalega:\n\n* Kaunsa function pehle execute karna hai.\n* Function complete hone ke baad kahan return karna hai.\n* Kis Execution Context ko active rakhna hai.\n* Kis context ko remove karna hai.\n\nIsliye Call Stack JavaScript ke execution ko sequence me aur correctly manage karta hai.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Call Stack (CS)\n\nCall Stack ek **LIFO (Last In, First Out)** data structure hai.\n\nIsme JavaScript Engine **Execution Contexts** ko push aur pop karta hai.\n\n### Kaam\n\n* Jab program start hota hai, **Global Execution Context** stack me push hota hai.\n* Jab koi function call hota hai, uska **Function Execution Context** stack ke top par push hota hai.\n* Function ka execution complete hone ke baad uska Execution Context stack se pop (destroy) ho jata hai.\n* Is process se JavaScript ko pata chalta hai ki kaunsa code pehle execute hoga aur kaunsa baad me.\n\n### Call Stack ko manager kyu bolte hain?\n\nCall Stack decide karta hai:\n\n* Kaunsa function abhi execute hoga.\n* Kaunsa function wait karega.\n* Execution complete hone par kaunsa context remove hoga.\n* Control kis context ko wapas dena hai.\n\n### Agar Call Stack na ho\n\nJavaScript Engine ko ye pata hi nahi chalega:\n\n* Kaunsa function pehle execute karna hai.\n* Function complete hone ke baad kahan return karna hai.\n* Kis Execution Context ko active rakhna hai.\n* Kis context ko remove karna hai.\n\nIsliye Call Stack JavaScript ke execution ko sequence me aur correctly manage karta hai.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vI5WvVroGYp6VklokDnSk",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 5541.984738729752,
      "y": 1850.9462668396131,
      "width": 2959.394654350963,
      "height": 4090.890216812129,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
