      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783255130232,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sabse simple rule\n\nJab bhi kisi function ke andar dusra function call hota hai:\n\nCurrent function pause ho jata hai.\nNaya function execute hota hai.\nNaya function complete hota hai.\nControl wapas purane function ki next line par aa jata hai.\n\nIsi wajah se JavaScript ko single-threaded language kehte hain—ek\ntime par sirf ek hi Execution Context actively execute hota hai.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sabse simple rule\n\nJab bhi kisi function ke andar dusra function call hota hai:\n\nCurrent function pause ho jata hai.\nNaya function execute hota hai.\nNaya function complete hota hai.\nControl wapas purane function ki next line par aa jata hai.\n\nIsi wajah se JavaScript ko single-threaded language kehte hain—ek time par sirf ek hi Execution Context actively execute hota hai.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
