    {
      "id": "RLYGbWwwUXAOiyEBJdnyZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9222.147831783011,
      "y": 14237.587740257713,
      "width": 1804.0211181640625,
      "height": 840,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b41",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 299882102,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 1913352810,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783453589078,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| **Feature**                 | **Variable Environment (VarEnv)**              | **Lexical Environment (LexEnv)**                     |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| Stores                      | `var` variables and Function Declarations      | `let`, `const`, class declarations                   |\n\n| Introduced For              | ES5 (`var`)                                    | ES6 (`let`, `const`)                                 |\n\n| Hoisting                    | `var` → `undefined`, Functions → fully hoisted | `let`/`const` → hoisted but uninitialized (TDZ)      |\n\n| Initial State               | Variables initialized with `undefined`         | Variables remain **uninitialized**                   |\n\n| TDZ                         | ❌ No                                           | ✅ Yes                                                |\n\n| Scope                       | Function Scope / Global Scope                  | Block Scope                                          |\n\n| Redeclaration               | `var` can be redeclared                        | `let`/`const` cannot be redeclared in the same scope |\n\n| Environment Record          | Yes                                            | Yes                                                  |\n\n| Outer Environment Reference | Yes                                            | Yes                                                  |\n\n| Created During              | Memory Creation Phase                          | Memory Creation Phase                                |\n\n| Used During                 | Execution Phase                                | Execution Phase                                      |\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| **Feature**                 | **Variable Environment (VarEnv)**              | **Lexical Environment (LexEnv)**                     |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| Stores                      | `var` variables and Function Declarations      | `let`, `const`, class declarations                   |\n\n| Introduced For              | ES5 (`var`)                                    | ES6 (`let`, `const`)                                 |\n\n| Hoisting                    | `var` → `undefined`, Functions → fully hoisted | `let`/`const` → hoisted but uninitialized (TDZ)      |\n\n| Initial State               | Variables initialized with `undefined`         | Variables remain **uninitialized**                   |\n\n| TDZ                         | ❌ No                                           | ✅ Yes                                                |\n\n| Scope                       | Function Scope / Global Scope                  | Block Scope                                          |\n\n| Redeclaration               | `var` can be redeclared                        | `let`/`const` cannot be redeclared in the same scope |\n\n| Environment Record          | Yes                                            | Yes                                                  |\n\n| Outer Environment Reference | Yes                                            | Yes                                                  |\n\n| Created During              | Memory Creation Phase                          | Memory Creation Phase                                |\n\n| Used During                 | Execution Phase                                | Execution Phase                                      |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sQnF3mNWKfbAklN8Lis_A",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 9185.435179628574,
      "y": 14211.638527435567,
      "width": 1900.2830463613172,
