    },
    {
      "id": "Evm6sa0x7OD6dHSBo2GKk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9355.788004993834,
      "y": 15525.073174831723,
      "width": 2061.05078125,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b43",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1624057654,
      "version": 10,
      "versionNonce": 1322098026,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783453657128,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| **Feature**                       | **Declaration**                                      | **Initialization**                                        |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Meaning                           | Creating a variable (introducing its name).          | Giving the variable its first value.                      |\n\n| Purpose                           | Tells JavaScript that the variable exists.           | Assigns the initial value to the variable.                |\n\n| Happens During                    | Memory Creation Phase (conceptually for hoisting)    | Execution Phase (when the declaration statement executes) \n\n| Value After Step                  | `var` → `undefined`<br>`let`/`const` → Uninitialized | Variable gets its actual value.                           |\n\n| Syntax                            | `var a;`<br>`let b;`                                 | `a = 10;`<br>`b = 20;`                                    |\n\n| Can Exist Without Initialization? | ✅ Yes (`var`, `let`)                                 | ❌ Initialization requires a declared variable.            |\n\n| `const`                           | Declaration must include initialization.             | Happens at the same time as declaration.                  |\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| **Feature**                       | **Declaration**                                      | **Initialization**                                        |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Meaning                           | Creating a variable (introducing its name).          | Giving the variable its first value.                      |\n\n| Purpose                           | Tells JavaScript that the variable exists.           | Assigns the initial value to the variable.                |\n\n| Happens During                    | Memory Creation Phase (conceptually for hoisting)    | Execution Phase (when the declaration statement executes) \n\n| Value After Step                  | `var` → `undefined`<br>`let`/`const` → Uninitialized | Variable gets its actual value.                           |\n\n| Syntax                            | `var a;`<br>`let b;`                                 | `a = 10;`<br>`b = 20;`                                    |\n\n| Can Exist Without Initialization? | ✅ Yes (`var`, `let`)                                 | ❌ Initialization requires a declared variable.            |\n\n| `const`                           | Declaration must include initialization.             | Happens at the same time as declaration.                  |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Tqvg4xmKgmVswQjtyA4HB",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 9336.366881378111,
