      "seed": 1922597151,
      "version": 291,
      "versionNonce": 175317009,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784065347453,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. TYPE CASTING :\nyeh kya krta hai  yeh appki type convert kar dega one to another manally . Power of converting it si in the hand of develoepr\n\nyou are reauired to use your 6 inbuilt funtion to do that .\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. TYPE CASTING :\nyeh kya krta hai  yeh appki type convert kar dega one to another manally . Power of converting it si in the hand of develoepr\n\nyou are reauired to use your 6 inbuilt funtion to do that .\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zCSdqVECUYTaNJKyVb4M4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13383.508335295184,
      "y": 10146.550202435581,
      "width": 1377.971435546875,
      "height": 3195,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 847581137,
      "version": 70,
      "versionNonce": 466649055,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784065457236,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Case 1: parseFloat()\nparseFloat(\"10.1adee\")\n\nOutput:\n\n10.1\n\nKyun?\n\nparseFloat() left se right padhta hai.\n\n1 ✅\n0 ✅\n. ✅\n1 ✅\na ❌ (yahin ruk gaya)\n\nJitna valid decimal number mila, utna return kar diya.\n\n\"10.1adee\"\n   ↑\n10.1 ✓\n     ↑\n'a' mila → stop\n\nIsliye output 10.1.\n\nCase 2: Number()\nNumber(\"10.1adee\")\n\nOutput:\n\nNaN\n\nKyun?\n\nNumber() poori string check karta hai.\n\nAgar ek bhi invalid character mil gaya (a), to kehta hai:\n\n\"Main is poori string ko number nahi bana sakta.\"\n\nIsliye output NaN.\n\nEk aur example\nparseInt(\"123abc\")\n\n➡️ 123\n\nNumber(\"123abc\")\n\n➡️ NaN\n\nRule yaad rakho\nMethod        Rule\nparseInt()        Jitna valid integer mile, utna le lo.\nparseFloat()        Jitna valid decimal number mile, utna le lo.\nNumber()        Puri string valid number honi chahiye, warna NaN.\nInterview me agar poochhe:\nparseFloat(\"99.5xyz\")\n\n➡️ 99.5\n\nNumber(\"99.5xyz\")\n\n➡️ NaN\n\nShortcut:\n\nparseInt() aur parseFloat() = \"Valid part milte hi le lo, invalid aaya to ruk jao.\"\nNumber() = \"Puri string valid honi chahiye, warna NaN.\"",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Case 1: parseFloat()\nparseFloat(\"10.1adee\")\n\nOutput:\n\n10.1\n\nKyun?\n\nparseFloat() left se right padhta hai.\n\n1 ✅\n0 ✅\n. ✅\n1 ✅\na ❌ (yahin ruk gaya)\n\nJitna valid decimal number mila, utna return kar diya.\n\n\"10.1adee\"\n   ↑\n10.1 ✓\n     ↑\n'a' mila → stop\n\nIsliye output 10.1.\n\nCase 2: Number()\nNumber(\"10.1adee\")\n\nOutput:\n\nNaN\n\nKyun?\n\nNumber() poori string check karta hai.\n\nAgar ek bhi invalid character mil gaya (a), to kehta hai:\n\n\"Main is poori string ko number nahi bana sakta.\"\n\nIsliye output NaN.\n\nEk aur example\nparseInt(\"123abc\")\n\n➡️ 123\n\nNumber(\"123abc\")\n\n➡️ NaN\n\nRule yaad rakho\nMethod        Rule\nparseInt()        Jitna valid integer mile, utna le lo.\nparseFloat()        Jitna valid decimal number mile, utna le lo.\nNumber()        Puri string valid number honi chahiye, warna NaN.\nInterview me agar poochhe:\nparseFloat(\"99.5xyz\")\n\n➡️ 99.5\n\nNumber(\"99.5xyz\")\n\n➡️ NaN\n\nShortcut:\n\nparseInt() aur parseFloat() = \"Valid part milte hi le lo, invalid aaya to ruk jao.\"\nNumber() = \"Puri string valid honi chahiye, warna NaN.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
