    },
    {
      "id": "LLZATC4FsRNZAI7KE6lNB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19617.6612294515,
      "y": 1596.8867390950547,
      "width": 1433.2591552734375,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ff8787",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b89",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 529177428,
      "version": 33,
      "versionNonce": 1552196692,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784511179776,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Higher Order Function (HOF)\n\n* **Higher Order Function** woh function hota hai jo **function ko argument ke roop me receive karta hai** ya **function return karta hai**.\n* Agar koi function in dono me se **koi ek** kaam karta hai, to use **Higher Order Function** kehte hain.\n\n### Callback se relation\n\n* Callback Function ka concept **Higher Order Function ki wajah se hi exist karta hai.**\n* Jab ek **Higher Order Function** kisi function ko argument me receive karta hai, to receive kiya gaya function **Callback Function** kehlata hai.\n\n### Yaad rakhne wali line\n\n**Higher Order Function receives/returns a function.**\n\n**Callback Function is the function that is passed to a Higher Order Function.**\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfunction main(callback) {   // Higher Order Function\n    callback();\n}\n\nmain(greet);                // greet becomes Callback Function\n```\n\n* `main` → **Higher Order Function**\n* `greet` → **Callback Function**\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Higher Order Function (HOF)\n\n* **Higher Order Function** woh function hota hai jo **function ko argument ke roop me receive karta hai** ya **function return karta hai**.\n* Agar koi function in dono me se **koi ek** kaam karta hai, to use **Higher Order Function** kehte hain.\n\n### Callback se relation\n\n* Callback Function ka concept **Higher Order Function ki wajah se hi exist karta hai.**\n* Jab ek **Higher Order Function** kisi function ko argument me receive karta hai, to receive kiya gaya function **Callback Function** kehlata hai.\n\n### Yaad rakhne wali line\n\n**Higher Order Function receives/returns a function.**\n\n**Callback Function is the function that is passed to a Higher Order Function.**\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfunction main(callback) {   // Higher Order Function\n    callback();\n}\n\nmain(greet);                // greet becomes Callback Function\n```\n\n* `main` → **Higher Order Function**\n* `greet` → **Callback Function**\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uL40VJLAOmyzlQbzdfib0",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 19594.327896118164,
      "y": 2064.6645253499373,
      "width": 664.4444783528634,
