      "seed": 610362964,
      "version": 32,
      "versionNonce": 21971436,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784513360886,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Inversion of Control (Callback Problem)\n\nNormal function me **poora control developer ke paas hota hai**. Main khud decide karta hoon:\n\n* Function kab execute karna hai.\n* Kitni baar execute karna hai.\n* Kis order me execute karna hai.\n\nLekin jab main apna **Callback Function** kisi doosre function (especially kisi **third-party library** ya built-in API) ko pass kar deta hoon, to callback ke execution ka control mere paas nahi rehta.\n\nAb receiving function ya library decide karti hai:\n\n* Callback **kab execute hoga**.\n* Callback **execute hoga bhi ya nahi**.\n* Callback **kitni baar execute hoga**.\n* Callback ko **kaunsa data pass kiya jayega**.\n\nAgar woh function kisi **third-party library** ka hai (jaise `fs.readFile()`), to main uska internal code bhi nahi dekh sakta aur na hi uske behavior ko control kar sakta hoon.\n\nIsi control ke developer se library ke paas chale jaane ko **Inversion of Control (IoC)** kehte hain.\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfs.readFile(\"data.txt\", function (err, data) {\n    console.log(data);\n});\n```\n\nYahan callback humne diya hai, lekin us callback ko **kab execute karna hai**, ye `fs.readFile()` decide karta hai, hum nahi.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Inversion of Control (Callback Problem)\n\nNormal function me **poora control developer ke paas hota hai**. Main khud decide karta hoon:\n\n* Function kab execute karna hai.\n* Kitni baar execute karna hai.\n* Kis order me execute karna hai.\n\nLekin jab main apna **Callback Function** kisi doosre function (especially kisi **third-party library** ya built-in API) ko pass kar deta hoon, to callback ke execution ka control mere paas nahi rehta.\n\nAb receiving function ya library decide karti hai:\n\n* Callback **kab execute hoga**.\n* Callback **execute hoga bhi ya nahi**.\n* Callback **kitni baar execute hoga**.\n* Callback ko **kaunsa data pass kiya jayega**.\n\nAgar woh function kisi **third-party library** ka hai (jaise `fs.readFile()`), to main uska internal code bhi nahi dekh sakta aur na hi uske behavior ko control kar sakta hoon.\n\nIsi control ke developer se library ke paas chale jaane ko **Inversion of Control (IoC)** kehte hain.\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfs.readFile(\"data.txt\", function (err, data) {\n    console.log(data);\n});\n```\n\nYahan callback humne diya hai, lekin us callback ko **kab execute karna hai**, ye `fs.readFile()` decide karta hai, hum nahi.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
