      "updated": 1784581514620,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Executor fucntion :\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Executor fucntion :\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kkCtkhtISplzL0kZiAgur",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 22087.592628479004,
      "y": 5085.185024295325,
      "width": 1323.51904296875,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2069328097,
      "version": 72,
      "versionNonce": 1455642497,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784581986027,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Executor Function\n\n**Executor Function decide karta hai ki Promise ko future me kya value milegi aur kab milegi.** Iske andar hum asynchronous operation \n(API call, file read, database query, timer, etc.) \nperform karte hain. Operation ke result ke basis par Executor decide karta hai ki `resolve()` call karna hai ya `reject()`.\n\nSimple words me:\n\n> **Promise ki future state aur result ko control karne ka kaam Executor Function karta hai.**\n\nExecutor Function ko Promise Constructor **2 functions provide karta hai**:\n\n### `resolve()`\n\n* `resolve()` ek function hai jo **Promise Constructor Executor Function ko pass karta hai**.\n* Jab asynchronous operation **successfully complete** ho jata hai, tab `resolve()` call kiya jata hai.\n* Ye Promise ki state **Pending → Fulfilled** kar deta hai.\n* `resolve(value)` me jo value pass karte ho, wahi value agle `.then()` ko milti hai.\n\n### `reject()`\n\n* `reject()` bhi ek function hai jo **Promise Constructor Executor Function ko pass karta hai**.\n* Jab asynchronous operation **fail** ho jata hai, tab `reject()` call kiya jata hai.\n* Ye Promise ki state **Pending → Rejected** kar deta hai.\n* `reject(error)` me jo error ya reason pass karte ho, wahi agle `.catch()` ko milta hai.\n\n### Interview One-Liner\n\n> **Executor Function asynchronous operation perform karta hai aur uske result ke basis par `resolve()` ya \n`reject()` call karke Promise ka future decide karta hai.**\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Executor Function\n\n**Executor Function decide karta hai ki Promise ko future me kya value milegi aur kab milegi.** Iske andar hum asynchronous operation \n(API call, file read, database query, timer, etc.) \nperform karte hain. Operation ke result ke basis par Executor decide karta hai ki `resolve()` call karna hai ya `reject()`.\n\nSimple words me:\n\n> **Promise ki future state aur result ko control karne ka kaam Executor Function karta hai.**\n\nExecutor Function ko Promise Constructor **2 functions provide karta hai**:\n\n### `resolve()`\n\n* `resolve()` ek function hai jo **Promise Constructor Executor Function ko pass karta hai**.\n* Jab asynchronous operation **successfully complete** ho jata hai, tab `resolve()` call kiya jata hai.\n* Ye Promise ki state **Pending → Fulfilled** kar deta hai.\n* `resolve(value)` me jo value pass karte ho, wahi value agle `.then()` ko milti hai.\n\n### `reject()`\n\n* `reject()` bhi ek function hai jo **Promise Constructor Executor Function ko pass karta hai**.\n* Jab asynchronous operation **fail** ho jata hai, tab `reject()` call kiya jata hai.\n* Ye Promise ki state **Pending → Rejected** kar deta hai.\n* `reject(error)` me jo error ya reason pass karte ho, wahi agle `.catch()` ko milta hai.\n\n### Interview One-Liner\n\n> **Executor Function asynchronous operation perform karta hai aur uske result ke basis par `resolve()` ya \n`reject()` call karke Promise ka future decide karta hai.**\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "U9NzYZNKwMpgKNE0zjySL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23659.81527455649,
      "y": 5195.833112382592,
      "width": 653.1795654296875,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1921524527,
      "version": 108,
      "versionNonce": 1200702881,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784581993705,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sabse Important Baat ⭐\n\nresolve() khud check nahi karta ki operation successful hui ya nahi.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sabse Important Baat ⭐\n\nresolve() khud check nahi karta ki operation successful hui ya nahi.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wvwEUgqEEPqA2sQU3qFKt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23786.507474263522,
      "y": 5341.4060036179435,
      "width": 168.1999053955078,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 778244449,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 946123119,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784582004312,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "if (success) {\n    resolve(data);\n} else {\n    reject(error);\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "if (success) {\n    resolve(data);\n} else {\n    reject(error);\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5NtRpUpr2veMEOUx7Vi0b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 23682.03695424399,
      "y": 5537.499524736108,
      "width": 485.23553466796875,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 514613679,
      "version": 17,
      "versionNonce": 381404143,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784582018296,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yani:\n\nExecutor async operation ka result dekhta hai.\nAgar result success hai → resolve() call karta hai.\nAgar result failure hai → reject() call karta hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yani:\n\nExecutor async operation ka result dekhta hai.\nAgar result success hai → resolve() call karta hai.\nAgar result failure hai → reject() call karta hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
