      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Promise Handlers\n\n**Promise Handlers** woh functions hote hain jo **Promise Object ki state change hone ka wait karte hain**. Jab Promise settle ho jata hai (Fulfilled ya Rejected), tab ye handlers execute hote hain aur Promise ka result ya error receive karte hain.\n\nInka kaam Promise ko control karna nahi, **Promise ke result ko handle karna** hota hai.\n\n---\n\n## `.then()`\n\n`.then()` ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **Pending → Fulfilled** hone ka wait karta hai.\nJab Promise successfully **Fulfilled** ho jata hai, tab `.then()` execute hota hai aur `resolve()` se pass hui value ko receive karta hai.\nAgar Promise abhi **Pending** hai, to `.then()` wait karta hai. Jaise hi Promise Fulfilled hota hai, `.then()` automatically execute ho jata hai.\nEk Promise chain me multiple `.then()` ho sakte hain. Isi concept ko **Promise Chaining** kehte hain.\n\n---\n\n## `.catch()`\n\n`.catch()` bhi ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **Pending → Rejected** hone ka wait karta hai.\nJab Promise **Rejected** ho jata hai ya Promise chain me kahin error aa jata hai, tab `.catch()` execute hota hai aur `reject()` se pass hua error receive karta hai.\nAgar Promise reject ho jaye, to uske baad wale normal `.then()` handlers execute nahi hote. Control seedha nearest `.catch()` me chala jata hai.\n\n---\n\n## `.finally()`\n\n`.finally()` ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **settle (Fulfilled ya Rejected)** hone ke baad execute hota hai.\nIsse Promise ka result ya error nahi milta. Iska use **cleanup work** ke liye kiya jata hai, jaise:\n* Loading spinner band karna\n* Database connection close karna\n* File close karna\n* Resources release karna\n\nYeh hamesha execute hota hai, chahe Promise **Fulfilled** ho ya **Rejected**.\n\n---\n\n# Interview One-Liners\n\n### `.then()`\n\n> `.then()` waits for the Promise to become **Fulfilled** and handles the value passed by `resolve()`.\n\n### `.catch()`\n\n> `.catch()` waits for the Promise to become **Rejected** and handles the error passed by `reject()` or any error thrown in the Promise chain.\n\n### `.finally()`\n\n> `.finally()` executes after the Promise is settled, whether it is **Fulfilled** or **Rejected**, and is mainly used for cleanup tasks.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Promise Handlers\n\n**Promise Handlers** woh functions hote hain jo **Promise Object ki state change hone ka wait karte hain**. Jab Promise settle ho jata hai (Fulfilled ya Rejected), tab ye handlers execute hote hain aur Promise ka result ya error receive karte hain.\n\nInka kaam Promise ko control karna nahi, **Promise ke result ko handle karna** hota hai.\n\n---\n\n## `.then()`\n\n`.then()` ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **Pending → Fulfilled** hone ka wait karta hai.\nJab Promise successfully **Fulfilled** ho jata hai, tab `.then()` execute hota hai aur `resolve()` se pass hui value ko receive karta hai.\nAgar Promise abhi **Pending** hai, to `.then()` wait karta hai. Jaise hi Promise Fulfilled hota hai, `.then()` automatically execute ho jata hai.\nEk Promise chain me multiple `.then()` ho sakte hain. Isi concept ko **Promise Chaining** kehte hain.\n\n---\n\n## `.catch()`\n\n`.catch()` bhi ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **Pending → Rejected** hone ka wait karta hai.\nJab Promise **Rejected** ho jata hai ya Promise chain me kahin error aa jata hai, tab `.catch()` execute hota hai aur `reject()` se pass hua error receive karta hai.\nAgar Promise reject ho jaye, to uske baad wale normal `.then()` handlers execute nahi hote. Control seedha nearest `.catch()` me chala jata hai.\n\n---\n\n## `.finally()`\n\n`.finally()` ek **Promise Handler Function** hai jo Promise ke **settle (Fulfilled ya Rejected)** hone ke baad execute hota hai.\nIsse Promise ka result ya error nahi milta. Iska use **cleanup work** ke liye kiya jata hai, jaise:\n* Loading spinner band karna\n* Database connection close karna\n* File close karna\n* Resources release karna\n\nYeh hamesha execute hota hai, chahe Promise **Fulfilled** ho ya **Rejected**.\n\n---\n\n# Interview One-Liners\n\n### `.then()`\n\n> `.then()` waits for the Promise to become **Fulfilled** and handles the value passed by `resolve()`.\n\n### `.catch()`\n\n> `.catch()` waits for the Promise to become **Rejected** and handles the error passed by `reject()` or any error thrown in the Promise chain.\n\n### `.finally()`\n\n> `.finally()` executes after the Promise is settled, whether it is **Fulfilled** or **Rejected**, and is mainly used for cleanup tasks.\n",
