    {
      "id": "_wZUQGErsR1aschP0bQFB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 22268.67471765812,
      "y": 7565.894912669766,
      "width": 757.1195068359375,
      "height": 3450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4dabf7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1917014447,
      "version": 129,
      "versionNonce": 662311535,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784583486510,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Promise Working (10 Steps)\n\n\n\nStep 1: Promise is Created\nconst promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    // Executor Function\n});\nnew Promise() call hota hai.\nPromise Constructor ek Promise Object create karta hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 2: Initial State = Pending\nPromise create hote hi uski initial state hoti hai:\n\nState  : Pending\nResult : undefined\nAbhi Promise ka result available nahi hota.\n\n\n\nStep 3: Executor Function Executes Immediately\nPromise create hote hi Executor Function immediately execute ho jata hai.\nnew Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    console.log(\"Executor Started\");\n});\n\nYahin par asynchronous operation start kiya jata hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 4: Asynchronous Operation Starts\nExecutor ke andar async task start hota hai.\nExamples:\nAPI Call\nDatabase Query\nFile Read\nTimer (setTimeout)\n\nPromise abhi bhi Pending state me hota hai.\n\n\n\n\n\nStep 5: Executor Checks the Result\nJab async operation complete hota hai, Executor uska result check karta hai.\nSuccess ?\n    │\nYes ──► resolve()\nNo  ──► reject()\nYahi Promise ka future decide karta hai.\n\n\n\nStep 6: Promise State Changes\nAgar\n\nresolve(data);\nto\nPending → Fulfilled\n\nAgar\nreject(error);\nto\nPending → Rejected\nPromise ab settled ho chuka hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 7: Promise Handlers Wait\nJab tak Promise Pending rehta hai:\n.then() wait karta hai.\n.catch() wait karta hai.\n.finally() bhi wait karta hai.\nYe handlers sirf register hote hain.\n\n\n\n\nStep 8: Appropriate Handler Executes\nAgar Promise Fulfilled hua:\nresolve()\n      │\n      ▼\n.then()\nAgar Promise Rejected hua:\nreject()\n      │\n      ▼\n.catch()\n\nHandler Promise ka value ya error receive karta hai.\n\n\n\n\n\nStep 9: Promise Chaining Continues\nHar .then() ek naya Promise return karta hai.\nIsliye:\n\nPromise\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n\nYe process chain ki tarah continue hoti rehti hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 10: .finally() Executes\nJab Promise Fulfilled ya Rejected kisi bhi state me settle ho jata hai:\nFulfilled\n      │\n      ├──► .then()\n      │\n      ▼\n.finally()\n\nOR\n\nRejected\n      │\n      ├──► .catch()\n      │\n      ▼\n.finally()\n\n.finally() cleanup tasks ke liye execute hota hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Promise Working (10 Steps)\n\n\n\nStep 1: Promise is Created\nconst promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    // Executor Function\n});\nnew Promise() call hota hai.\nPromise Constructor ek Promise Object create karta hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 2: Initial State = Pending\nPromise create hote hi uski initial state hoti hai:\n\nState  : Pending\nResult : undefined\nAbhi Promise ka result available nahi hota.\n\n\n\nStep 3: Executor Function Executes Immediately\nPromise create hote hi Executor Function immediately execute ho jata hai.\nnew Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    console.log(\"Executor Started\");\n});\n\nYahin par asynchronous operation start kiya jata hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 4: Asynchronous Operation Starts\nExecutor ke andar async task start hota hai.\nExamples:\nAPI Call\nDatabase Query\nFile Read\nTimer (setTimeout)\n\nPromise abhi bhi Pending state me hota hai.\n\n\n\n\n\nStep 5: Executor Checks the Result\nJab async operation complete hota hai, Executor uska result check karta hai.\nSuccess ?\n    │\nYes ──► resolve()\nNo  ──► reject()\nYahi Promise ka future decide karta hai.\n\n\n\nStep 6: Promise State Changes\nAgar\n\nresolve(data);\nto\nPending → Fulfilled\n\nAgar\nreject(error);\nto\nPending → Rejected\nPromise ab settled ho chuka hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 7: Promise Handlers Wait\nJab tak Promise Pending rehta hai:\n.then() wait karta hai.\n.catch() wait karta hai.\n.finally() bhi wait karta hai.\nYe handlers sirf register hote hain.\n\n\n\n\nStep 8: Appropriate Handler Executes\nAgar Promise Fulfilled hua:\nresolve()\n      │\n      ▼\n.then()\nAgar Promise Rejected hua:\nreject()\n      │\n      ▼\n.catch()\n\nHandler Promise ka value ya error receive karta hai.\n\n\n\n\n\nStep 9: Promise Chaining Continues\nHar .then() ek naya Promise return karta hai.\nIsliye:\n\nPromise\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n\nYe process chain ki tarah continue hoti rehti hai.\n\n\n\n\nStep 10: .finally() Executes\nJab Promise Fulfilled ya Rejected kisi bhi state me settle ho jata hai:\nFulfilled\n      │\n      ├──► .then()\n      │\n      ▼\n.finally()\n\nOR\n\nRejected\n      │\n      ├──► .catch()\n      │\n      ▼\n.finally()\n\n.finally() cleanup tasks ke liye execute hota hai.",
