      "seed": 1768981583,
      "version": 664,
      "versionNonce": 1559129775,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784584628350,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Error Handling in Promises\n\nPromise me **Error Handling** ka ek built-in mechanism hota hai. Agar Promise chain ke kisi bhi step par **Promise reject ho jaye** ya **koi error throw ho jaye**, to JavaScript us error ko automatically\n**Rejected** state me convert kar deta hai.\n\nUske baad control seedha nearest **`.catch()`** handler ke paas chala jata hai. `.catch()` us error ko receive karke handle karta hai.\n\nJab Promise **Rejected** ho jata hai, to uske baad wale normal **`.then()`** handlers execute nahi hote. JavaScript unhe skip kar deta hai aur chain ko seedha `.catch()` tak le jata hai. Is process ko **Error\nPropagation** kehte hain.\n\nError handle hone ke baad, agar `.finally()` present ho, to wo hamesha execute hota hai, chahe Promise **Fulfilled** hua ho ya **Rejected**.\n\n### Flow\n\n```text\nPromise\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n   │\nError\n   │\n   ▼\nPromise → Rejected\n   │\n   ▼\nRemaining .then() Skipped\n   │\n   ▼\n.catch()\n   │\n   ▼\n.finally()\n```\n\n### Interview One-Liner\n\n> **Promise Error Handling is a mechanism in which any rejection or error occurring anywhere in the Promise chain automatically propagates to the nearest `.catch()`. The remaining `.then()` handlers are skipped,\nwhile `.finally()` always executes.**\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Error Handling in Promises\n\nPromise me **Error Handling** ka ek built-in mechanism hota hai. Agar Promise chain ke kisi bhi step par **Promise reject ho jaye** ya **koi error throw ho jaye**, to JavaScript us error ko automatically **Rejected** state me convert kar deta hai.\n\nUske baad control seedha nearest **`.catch()`** handler ke paas chala jata hai. `.catch()` us error ko receive karke handle karta hai.\n\nJab Promise **Rejected** ho jata hai, to uske baad wale normal **`.then()`** handlers execute nahi hote. JavaScript unhe skip kar deta hai aur chain ko seedha `.catch()` tak le jata hai. Is process ko **Error Propagation** kehte hain.\n\nError handle hone ke baad, agar `.finally()` present ho, to wo hamesha execute hota hai, chahe Promise **Fulfilled** hua ho ya **Rejected**.\n\n### Flow\n\n```text\nPromise\n   │\n.then()\n   │\n.then()\n   │\nError\n   │\n   ▼\nPromise → Rejected\n   │\n   ▼\nRemaining .then() Skipped\n   │\n   ▼\n.catch()\n   │\n   ▼\n.finally()\n```\n\n### Interview One-Liner\n\n> **Promise Error Handling is a mechanism in which any rejection or error occurring anywhere in the Promise chain automatically propagates to the nearest `.catch()`. The remaining `.then()` handlers are skipped, while `.finally()` always executes.**\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
