      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784609740545,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ab dekho baki ka code normal chalega but jo code hoga async mei woh reslove hone ke abdd hi chalega jab woh resolve state await\n\nkeyword tak chale jayegi ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ab dekho baki ka code normal chalega but jo code hoga async mei woh reslove hone ke abdd hi chalega jab woh resolve state await\n\nkeyword tak chale jayegi ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "8vm_d4wxLg8aeJzjDFAni",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 25691.790599847955,
      "y": 5034.009143565453,
      "width": 1623.0467529296875,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffa94d",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1208773007,
      "version": 962,
      "versionNonce": 948698817,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784610473974,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "try catch appka error handling technique hai async / await ka jo bacully appke error se deal akrne ke liye use hota hai \n\n\ntry : woh code dalo jo risky code hai -> success bhi ho skta hai  and failure bhi ho sakta hai \n\ncatch : agar appna promise reject ho jaye / ya code mai error a jeye toh isme ayega\n\n\nNOW see .then appka dekhne se lagta hai  ke callback mecahnishm abhi katam nai hua / chahe uske padd .catch hai jo \n\ncentralized error handle karne ke liye use hota hai ->>\n\n\nbut the thing is that -> ke .then() bht sare ho jate hai \n\nfucntionalutu same hai dono ki bas likhna ka tarike more cleaner and sync code lagta hai in try catch .\n\n\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "try catch appka error handling technique hai async / await ka jo bacully appke error se deal akrne ke liye use hota hai \n\n\ntry : woh code dalo jo risky code hai -> success bhi ho skta hai  and failure bhi ho sakta hai \n\ncatch : agar appna promise reject ho jaye / ya code mai error a jeye toh isme ayega\n\n\nNOW see .then appka dekhne se lagta hai  ke callback mecahnishm abhi katam nai hua / chahe uske padd .catch hai jo \n\ncentralized error handle karne ke liye use hota hai ->>\n\n\nbut the thing is that -> ke .then() bht sare ho jate hai \n\nfucntionalutu same hai dono ki bas likhna ka tarike more cleaner and sync code lagta hai in try catch .\n\n\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mWXNlvESsRxZQ_CHGbVaz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 25653.444271112603,
      "y": 5677.88936668957,
      "width": 1434.6630859375,
      "height": 770,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#a18072",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 675944001,
      "version": 48,
      "versionNonce": 1798897697,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784610555197,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| Feature                   | `try...catch`                      | `.catch()`                             |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n\n| Type                      | JavaScript statement               | Promise method                         |\n\n| Use                       | Error handle karne ke liye         | Promise rejection handle karne ke liye |\n\n| Works With                | Synchronous code + `async/await`   | Promises (`.then()`)                   |\n\n| Handles Sync Errors       | ✅ Yes                              | ❌ No                                   |\n\n| Handles Promise Rejection | ✅ Yes (with `await`)               | ✅ Yes                                  |\n\n\n| Requires `async`          | Sirf `await` use karte time        | ❌ No                                   |\n\n| Syntax                    | `try { ... } catch(err) { ... }`   | `promise.catch(err => { ... })`        |\n\n| Readability               | `async/await` ke saath zyada clean | Promise chaining me use hota hai       |\n\n| Best Use Case             | Modern `async/await` code          | `.then()` based Promise code           |\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| Feature                   | `try...catch`                      | `.catch()`                             |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n\n| Type                      | JavaScript statement               | Promise method                         |\n\n| Use                       | Error handle karne ke liye         | Promise rejection handle karne ke liye |\n\n| Works With                | Synchronous code + `async/await`   | Promises (`.then()`)                   |\n\n| Handles Sync Errors       | ✅ Yes                              | ❌ No                                   |\n\n| Handles Promise Rejection | ✅ Yes (with `await`)               | ✅ Yes                                  |\n\n\n| Requires `async`          | Sirf `await` use karte time        | ❌ No                                   |\n\n| Syntax                    | `try { ... } catch(err) { ... }`   | `promise.catch(err => { ... })`        |\n\n| Readability               | `async/await` ke saath zyada clean | Promise chaining me use hota hai       |\n\n| Best Use Case             | Modern `async/await` code          | `.then()` based Promise code           |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "n-MhU-zjikevvebK10AcM",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 25636.23502733819,
      "y": 4974.842428345285,
      "width": 1828.8627624511719,
      "height": 1540.5380249023438,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#a18072",
