      "updated": 1784753585059,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "yeh woh fucntion hote hai jinko ham treat karta hai as nromal values . \n\nin fucntion ko treat kiya jata hai normla values sotred in varaibles  \n\n\nAISE HAM kyo karte hai as to give develoeps a little buit more flexibility to deal wtih the fucntions \n\n1: sotre in the form of varaible\n\n2: passsed as the argment to another funtion\n\n3: iska memory referce depend kargea on the varibel you used .  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "yeh woh fucntion hote hai jinko ham treat karta hai as nromal values . \n\nin fucntion ko treat kiya jata hai normla values sotred in varaibles  \n\n\nAISE HAM kyo karte hai as to give develoeps a little buit more flexibility to deal wtih the fucntions \n\n1: sotre in the form of varaible\n\n2: passsed as the argment to another funtion\n\n3: iska memory referce depend kargea on the varibel you used .  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OJ9S0jE8ic1QxlFl4XATI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30039.118793954618,
      "y": 13142.05917504542,
      "width": 1601.20166015625,
      "height": 2025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1790522049,
      "version": 68,
      "versionNonce": 1511982433,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784753642962,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Variable me Store\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nconst x = greet;\n\nx();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function ko variable me store kiya.\n\n2. Argument ki tarah Pass\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfunction execute(fn) {\n    fn();\n}\n\nexecute(greet);\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function ko dusre function ke andar bheja.\n\n3. Function Return Karna\nfunction outer() {\n\n    return function () {\n        console.log(\"Hello\");\n    };\n\n}\n\nconst x = outer();\n\nx();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function return hua.\n\n4. Array me Store\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nconst arr = [greet];\n\narr[0]();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n5. Object me Store\nconst obj = {\n\n    greet: function () {\n        console.log(\"Hello\");\n    }\n\n};\n\nobj.greet();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\nInterview Definition ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nA language is said to support first-class functions if functions can be treated like any other value. They can be assigned to variables, passed as arguments,\nreturned from other functions, and stored in arrays or objects.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Variable me Store\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nconst x = greet;\n\nx();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function ko variable me store kiya.\n\n2. Argument ki tarah Pass\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nfunction execute(fn) {\n    fn();\n}\n\nexecute(greet);\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function ko dusre function ke andar bheja.\n\n3. Function Return Karna\nfunction outer() {\n\n    return function () {\n        console.log(\"Hello\");\n    };\n\n}\n\nconst x = outer();\n\nx();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n\nYahan function return hua.\n\n4. Array me Store\nfunction greet() {\n    console.log(\"Hello\");\n}\n\nconst arr = [greet];\n\narr[0]();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\n5. Object me Store\nconst obj = {\n\n    greet: function () {\n        console.log(\"Hello\");\n    }\n\n};\n\nobj.greet();\n\nOutput\n\nHello\nInterview Definition ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nA language is said to support first-class functions if functions can be treated like any other value. They can be assigned to variables, passed as arguments, returned from other functions, and stored in arrays or objects.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
