      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784855811494,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## DOM (Document Object Model)\n\nDOM ek **Conceptual (Logical) Representation** hai HTML document ki, jise browser aasani se **understand, store aur process**\nkar sake.\n\nYahan **Conceptual Representation (CR)** ka matlab **diagram ya flowchart banana nahi hai**. Iska matlab hai HTML document ko\n**tree-like logical structure (Object Model)** mein represent karna.\n\nBrowser HTML document ko **parse** karta hai aur usse **DOM Tree** mein convert karta hai. Is DOM Tree mein har HTML\nelement ek **node** hota hai. Is tree mein **Root Node, Parent Node, Child Node aur Leaf Node** hote hain.\n\nYe logical tree JavaScript ko kisi bhi element tak easily pahunchne (access), usse read karne, modify karne, naya element add karne\nya remove karne ki facility deta hai.\n\nSimple words mein:\n\n**HTML → Browser Parse → DOM Tree → JavaScript DOM ko manipulate karti hai → Browser Updated UI dikhata hai.**\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## DOM (Document Object Model)\n\nDOM ek **Conceptual (Logical) Representation** hai HTML document ki, jise browser aasani se **understand, store aur process** kar sake.\n\nYahan **Conceptual Representation (CR)** ka matlab **diagram ya flowchart banana nahi hai**. Iska matlab hai HTML document ko **tree-like logical structure (Object Model)** mein represent karna.\n\nBrowser HTML document ko **parse** karta hai aur usse **DOM Tree** mein convert karta hai. Is DOM Tree mein har HTML element ek **node** hota hai. Is tree mein **Root Node, Parent Node, Child Node aur Leaf Node** hote hain.\n\nYe logical tree JavaScript ko kisi bhi element tak easily pahunchne (access), usse read karne, modify karne, naya element add karne ya remove karne ki facility deta hai.\n\nSimple words mein:\n\n**HTML → Browser Parse → DOM Tree → JavaScript DOM ko manipulate karti hai → Browser Updated UI dikhata hai.**\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "htN9Szvt07SWgWSyF4SbJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 31869.87883282751,
      "y": -3291.3103129624915,
      "width": 1245.7723999023438,
      "height": 2695,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bDg",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1498025861,
      "version": 168,
      "versionNonce": 1486439877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784855948342,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## DOM ki Zarurat Kyu Padi?\n\nDekho, shuru mein sirf **HTML aur CSS** the.\n\n* **HTML** webpage ka structure banata tha.\n* **CSS** us webpage ko style karta tha.\n* Lekin webpage majorly **static** hota tha. User kuch bhi kare, page khud se change nahi\nhota tha.\n\nFir **JavaScript (JS)** aayi.\n\nAb JS ka kaam tha webpage ko **interactive** banana.\n\nJaise:\n\n* Button click hone par text change ho.\n* Form submit ho.\n* Image change ho.\n* Naya element add ho.\n* Kisi element ko remove ya hide karna ho.\n\nAb problem ye thi ki JS ko **kaise pata chalega ki HTML ke kis element par change karna\nhai?**\n\nJavaScript **direct HTML file ko modify nahi karti**.\n\nJS hamesha **objects** ke saath kaam karti hai. Isliye browser ko HTML ko aise format\nmein convert karna pada jise JavaScript easily samajh sake.\n\n### Browser Behind the Scenes\n\n1. Browser HTML document ko receive karta hai.\n2. Browser HTML ko **parse** karta hai.\n3. Parsing ke baad browser HTML ko ek **tree-like structure** mein convert karta hai.\n4. Is tree mein har HTML element ek **Node** hota hai.\n5. Tree ka ek **Root Node** hota hai aur uske andar **Parent Nodes, Child Nodes aur\nLeaf Nodes** hote hain.\n6. Browser is poori tree ko **memory** mein **JavaScript Objects** ke form mein store\nkarta hai.\n7. Isi tree-like object structure ko **DOM (Document Object Model)** kehte hain.\n\nAb kyunki ye JavaScript objects hote hain, JS inke **properties (keys)** aur **values** ko\naccess kar sakti hai.\n\nIsi wajah se JavaScript kisi bhi element ko:\n\n* Read kar sakti hai.\n* Modify kar sakti hai.\n* Naya element add kar sakti hai.\n* Existing element delete kar sakti hai.\n* Attributes aur styles update kar sakti hai.\n* Events (click, input, submit) handle kar sakti hai.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML + CSS (Static Page)\n\n↓\n\nBrowser HTML Parse karta hai\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree (JavaScript Objects in Memory)\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript DOM ko access karti hai\n\n↓\n\nRead / Add / Update / Delete\n\n↓\n\nBrowser Updated UI dikha deta hai.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## DOM ki Zarurat Kyu Padi?\n\nDekho, shuru mein sirf **HTML aur CSS** the.\n\n* **HTML** webpage ka structure banata tha.\n* **CSS** us webpage ko style karta tha.\n* Lekin webpage majorly **static** hota tha. User kuch bhi kare, page khud se change nahi hota tha.\n\nFir **JavaScript (JS)** aayi.\n\nAb JS ka kaam tha webpage ko **interactive** banana.\n\nJaise:\n\n* Button click hone par text change ho.\n* Form submit ho.\n* Image change ho.\n* Naya element add ho.\n* Kisi element ko remove ya hide karna ho.\n\nAb problem ye thi ki JS ko **kaise pata chalega ki HTML ke kis element par change karna hai?**\n\nJavaScript **direct HTML file ko modify nahi karti**.\n\nJS hamesha **objects** ke saath kaam karti hai. Isliye browser ko HTML ko aise format mein convert karna pada jise JavaScript easily samajh sake.\n\n### Browser Behind the Scenes\n\n1. Browser HTML document ko receive karta hai.\n2. Browser HTML ko **parse** karta hai.\n3. Parsing ke baad browser HTML ko ek **tree-like structure** mein convert karta hai.\n4. Is tree mein har HTML element ek **Node** hota hai.\n5. Tree ka ek **Root Node** hota hai aur uske andar **Parent Nodes, Child Nodes aur Leaf Nodes** hote hain.\n6. Browser is poori tree ko **memory** mein **JavaScript Objects** ke form mein store karta hai.\n7. Isi tree-like object structure ko **DOM (Document Object Model)** kehte hain.\n\nAb kyunki ye JavaScript objects hote hain, JS inke **properties (keys)** aur **values** ko access kar sakti hai.\n\nIsi wajah se JavaScript kisi bhi element ko:\n\n* Read kar sakti hai.\n* Modify kar sakti hai.\n* Naya element add kar sakti hai.\n* Existing element delete kar sakti hai.\n* Attributes aur styles update kar sakti hai.\n* Events (click, input, submit) handle kar sakti hai.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML + CSS (Static Page)\n\n↓\n\nBrowser HTML Parse karta hai\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree (JavaScript Objects in Memory)\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript DOM ko access karti hai\n\n↓\n\nRead / Add / Update / Delete\n\n↓\n\nBrowser Updated UI dikha deta hai.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
