      "seed": 1839204907,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 69092549,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784856795228,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Document Object\n\n* [ ] **Document Object** basically **DOM ka root object** hota hai. Isi object ke through hum poore DOM ko access aur control kar sakte hain.\n\nBrowser jab *HTML document ko parse karta hai, tab woh ek ****DOM Tree**** banata hai.* Is DOM Tree ka top-level object **Document Object** hota hai.\n\nYe **Document Object browser ki memory mein JavaScript Object** ke form mein store hota hai.\n\nJavaScript directly HTML file ke saath kaam nahi karti. JavaScript **Document Object** ke through DOM ke elements ko access karti hai.\n\nIsi wajah se hum likhte hain:\n\n```javascript\ndocument.getElementById(\"title\")\ndocument.querySelector(\".box\")\ndocument.createElement(\"div\")\n```\n\nYahan `document` hi woh root object hai jahan se JavaScript poore DOM ko traverse (navigate) karti hai.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML Document\n\n↓\n\nBrowser Parse\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree\n\n↓\n\n**Document Object (Root Object)**\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript\n\n↓\n\nRead / Access / Add / Update / Delete Elements\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Document Object\n\n* [ ] **Document Object** basically **DOM ka root object** hota hai. Isi object ke through hum poore DOM ko access aur control kar sakte hain.\n\nBrowser jab *HTML document ko parse karta hai, tab woh ek ****DOM Tree**** banata hai.* Is DOM Tree ka top-level object **Document Object** hota hai.\n\nYe **Document Object browser ki memory mein JavaScript Object** ke form mein store hota hai.\n\nJavaScript directly HTML file ke saath kaam nahi karti. JavaScript **Document Object** ke through DOM ke elements ko access karti hai.\n\nIsi wajah se hum likhte hain:\n\n```javascript\ndocument.getElementById(\"title\")\ndocument.querySelector(\".box\")\ndocument.createElement(\"div\")\n```\n\nYahan `document` hi woh root object hai jahan se JavaScript poore DOM ko traverse (navigate) karti hai.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML Document\n\n↓\n\nBrowser Parse\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree\n\n↓\n\n**Document Object (Root Object)**\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript\n\n↓\n\nRead / Access / Add / Update / Delete Elements\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
