      "updated": 1784857488548,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## DOM Tree\n\nThe **DOM Tree** is a tree-like structure that is created after the browser parses the **HTML document**.\n\nIt consists of **Root Node, Parent Nodes, Child Nodes, and Leaf Nodes**.\n\nThis tree establishes a **parent-child relationship** between all HTML elements.\n\n The **Document Object** is the **root object** of the DOM. It is the entry point through which you can access and control the entire HTML DOM.\n\nThe DOM Tree is created during the **HTML parsing phase**. It helps the browser and JavaScript locate, access, and manipulate the desired HTML elements efficiently.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML Document \n\n↓\n \nBrowser Parses HTML\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree Created\n\n↓\n\nDocument Object (Root Object)\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript Accesses DOM\n\n↓\n\nRead / Add / Update / Delete Elements\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## DOM Tree\n\nThe **DOM Tree** is a tree-like structure that is created after the browser parses the **HTML document**.\n\nIt consists of **Root Node, Parent Nodes, Child Nodes, and Leaf Nodes**.\n\nThis tree establishes a **parent-child relationship** between all HTML elements.\n\n The **Document Object** is the **root object** of the DOM. It is the entry point through which you can access and control the entire HTML DOM.\n\nThe DOM Tree is created during the **HTML parsing phase**. It helps the browser and JavaScript locate, access, and manipulate the desired HTML elements efficiently.\n\n### Simple Flow\n\nHTML Document \n\n↓\n \nBrowser Parses HTML\n\n↓\n\nDOM Tree Created\n\n↓\n\nDocument Object (Root Object)\n\n↓\n\nJavaScript Accesses DOM\n\n↓\n\nRead / Add / Update / Delete Elements\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
