    {
      "id": "3ZVHADx6C9Qw7yPoIksvj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 35498.84691344504,
      "y": -2329.859984881236,
      "width": 1979.349609375,
      "height": 830.0138621803661,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4dabf7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bH6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1186866805,
      "version": 47,
      "versionNonce": 223286267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785239945806,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| **Class**                                            | **Object**                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n\n| A class is a **blueprint** or template.              | An object is a **real instance** of a class.                |\n\n| It defines properties and methods.                   | It contains actual values for those properties and methods. |\n\n| Memory is **not allocated** when a class is created. | Memory **is allocated** when an object is created.          |\n\n| A class is a **logical entity**.                     | An object is a **physical entity**.                         |\n\n| One class can create **many objects**.               | An object belongs to **one class**.                         |\n\n| It does not represent a real-world entity directly.  | It represents a **real-world entity**.                      |\n\n| Created using the `class` keyword.                   | Created using the `new` keyword.                            |\n\n| Example: `class Student {}`                          | Example: `const s1 = new Student()`                         |\n",
      "fontSize": 34.947952091804886,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| **Class**                                            | **Object**                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n\n| A class is a **blueprint** or template.              | An object is a **real instance** of a class.                |\n\n| It defines properties and methods.                   | It contains actual values for those properties and methods. |\n\n| Memory is **not allocated** when a class is created. | Memory **is allocated** when an object is created.          |\n\n| A class is a **logical entity**.                     | An object is a **physical entity**.                         |\n\n| One class can create **many objects**.               | An object belongs to **one class**.                         |\n\n| It does not represent a real-world entity directly.  | It represents a **real-world entity**.                      |\n\n| Created using the `class` keyword.                   | Created using the `new` keyword.                            |\n\n| Example: `class Student {}`                          | Example: `const s1 = new Student()`                         |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
