      "updated": 1785249155406,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "conjstrctor: ::\n\n1> class ke andar defined hota hai  -->> abb jaise hi yeh new keyword dekhega waise hi call ho jayega , matalb jab ham new object create krege constructor appne app call ho jaa hai .\n\n\n\nWORKING STEPS OF CONSTRUCTOR ::\n\n     ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "conjstrctor: ::\n\n1> class ke andar defined hota hai  -->> abb jaise hi yeh new keyword dekhega waise hi call ho jayega , matalb jab ham new object create krege constructor appne app call ho jaa hai .\n\n\n\nWORKING STEPS OF CONSTRUCTOR ::\n\n     ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GshPMzraaUXncG5vJrIAN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 38146.2843893553,
      "y": -3514.7531417480095,
      "width": 1853.6024302402463,
      "height": 2044.0288139097345,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f783ac",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 768318677,
      "version": 95,
      "versionNonce": 180366837,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785249556540,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Step 1\nnew Student(\"Amar\", 21)\n\n➡️ new keyword execute hua.\n\nStep 2\n\nnew kya karta hai?\n\n✅ Memory mein ek naya empty object banata hai.\n{}\n\n\nStep 3\n\nUs object ka this constructor ke andar point kar diya jata hai.\n\nthis -----> {}\n\n\nStep 4\n\nConstructor automatically call hota hai.\n\nconstructor(\"Amar\",21)\n\n\nStep 5\n\nYe lines execute hoti hain.\n\nthis.name = \"Amar\";\nthis.age = 21;\n\nObject ban gaya\n\n{\n   name: \"Amar\",\n   age: 21\n}\n\n\nStep 6\n\nnew us object ka reference return kar deta hai.\n\ns1\n │\n ▼\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\nInterview Definition ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nConstructor is a special method inside a class that is automatically invoked when an object is created using the new keyword. It is\nused to initialize the object's properties and set up",
      "fontSize": 28.688123703996272,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Step 1\nnew Student(\"Amar\", 21)\n\n➡️ new keyword execute hua.\n\nStep 2\n\nnew kya karta hai?\n\n✅ Memory mein ek naya empty object banata hai.\n{}\n\n\nStep 3\n\nUs object ka this constructor ke andar point kar diya jata hai.\n\nthis -----> {}\n\n\nStep 4\n\nConstructor automatically call hota hai.\n\nconstructor(\"Amar\",21)\n\n\nStep 5\n\nYe lines execute hoti hain.\n\nthis.name = \"Amar\";\nthis.age = 21;\n\nObject ban gaya\n\n{\n   name: \"Amar\",\n   age: 21\n}\n\n\nStep 6\n\nnew us object ka reference return kar deta hai.\n\ns1\n │\n ▼\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\nInterview Definition ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nConstructor is a special method inside a class that is automatically invoked when an object is created using the new keyword. It is used to initialize the object's properties and set up",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
