    {
      "id": "XaFrBbntxJdo0_NMndDlc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 41256.058795376186,
      "y": -6437.961026122503,
      "width": 926.5783081054688,
      "height": 5250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#da77f2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1633029397,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 316279811,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785419266231,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ Step 1: Class Create Karna\nclass Student {\n    constructor(name, age){\n        this.name = name;\n        this.age = age;\n    }\n}\nclass keyword se class banayi.\nConstructor define kiya.\nConstructor ke andar properties aur arguments likhe.\n\n👉 Abhi tak koi object create nahi hua.\n\n✅ Step 2: Class Memory Mein Register Hoti Hai\nclass Student { ... }\nJavaScript class ko memory mein register kar deta hai.\nConstructor bhi memory mein store ho jata hai.\n\nAbhi tak\n\n❌ Constructor call nahi hua.\n\n❌ Object create nahi hua.\n\n❌ Constructor ne kuch return nahi kiya.\n\nSirf class ready hai.\n\n✅ Step 3: new Keyword Milta Hai\nlet s1 = new Student(\"Amar\",21);\n\nJaise hi JavaScript ko new dikhta hai,\n\nsabse pehle\n\n(a) Ek naya empty object create hota hai\n{}\n\nYe future object hai.\n\n✅ Step 4: Prototype Link Set Hota Hai ⭐ (Missing Step)\n\nJavaScript is empty object ka hidden prototype\n\n__proto__\n\nko\n\nStudent.prototype\n\nse connect kar deta hai.\n\nIs wajah se object future mein methods access kar pata hai.\n\ns1\n |\n |__proto__\n      |\n      Student.prototype\n\nYe step bahut important hai.\n\n✅ Step 5: Constructor Automatically Call Hota Hai\n\nAb JavaScript internally kuch aisa karta hai\n\nStudent.call(emptyObject,\"Amar\",21);\n\nMatlab constructor automatically call hota hai.\n\nIsliye constructor ko manually call nahi karte.\n\n✅ Step 6: this Current Object Ko Refer Karta Hai\n\nAb constructor ke andar\n\nthis.name = name;\nthis.age = age;\n\nYaha\n\nthis\n\nabhi jo empty object bana tha usko refer karta hai.\n\nBefore\n\n{}\n\nAfter\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\nIsi step mein properties object ke andar store hoti hain.\n\n✅ Step 7: Constructor Finish Hota Hai\n\nJab constructor ka code execute ho jata hai,\n\ntab object complete ban chuka hota hai.\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\n\n✅ Step 8: Object Automatically Return Hota Hai ⭐ (Missing Step)\n\nAgar constructor khud explicitly koi object return nahi karta,\n\nto JavaScript automatically\n\nthis\n\nko return kar deta hai.\n\nInternally aisa hota hai\n\nreturn this;\n\nYe JavaScript khud karta hai.\n\n✅ Step 9: Returned Object Variable Mein Store Hota Hai\n\nAb\n\nlet s1 = new Student(\"Amar\",21);\n\nke andar\n\nreturn hua object\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\ns1 variable ke andar store ho jata hai.\n\ns1\n |\n ▼\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ Step 1: Class Create Karna\nclass Student {\n    constructor(name, age){\n        this.name = name;\n        this.age = age;\n    }\n}\nclass keyword se class banayi.\nConstructor define kiya.\nConstructor ke andar properties aur arguments likhe.\n\n👉 Abhi tak koi object create nahi hua.\n\n✅ Step 2: Class Memory Mein Register Hoti Hai\nclass Student { ... }\nJavaScript class ko memory mein register kar deta hai.\nConstructor bhi memory mein store ho jata hai.\n\nAbhi tak\n\n❌ Constructor call nahi hua.\n\n❌ Object create nahi hua.\n\n❌ Constructor ne kuch return nahi kiya.\n\nSirf class ready hai.\n\n✅ Step 3: new Keyword Milta Hai\nlet s1 = new Student(\"Amar\",21);\n\nJaise hi JavaScript ko new dikhta hai,\n\nsabse pehle\n\n(a) Ek naya empty object create hota hai\n{}\n\nYe future object hai.\n\n✅ Step 4: Prototype Link Set Hota Hai ⭐ (Missing Step)\n\nJavaScript is empty object ka hidden prototype\n\n__proto__\n\nko\n\nStudent.prototype\n\nse connect kar deta hai.\n\nIs wajah se object future mein methods access kar pata hai.\n\ns1\n |\n |__proto__\n      |\n      Student.prototype\n\nYe step bahut important hai.\n\n✅ Step 5: Constructor Automatically Call Hota Hai\n\nAb JavaScript internally kuch aisa karta hai\n\nStudent.call(emptyObject,\"Amar\",21);\n\nMatlab constructor automatically call hota hai.\n\nIsliye constructor ko manually call nahi karte.\n\n✅ Step 6: this Current Object Ko Refer Karta Hai\n\nAb constructor ke andar\n\nthis.name = name;\nthis.age = age;\n\nYaha\n\nthis\n\nabhi jo empty object bana tha usko refer karta hai.\n\nBefore\n\n{}\n\nAfter\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\nIsi step mein properties object ke andar store hoti hain.\n\n✅ Step 7: Constructor Finish Hota Hai\n\nJab constructor ka code execute ho jata hai,\n\ntab object complete ban chuka hota hai.\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\n\n✅ Step 8: Object Automatically Return Hota Hai ⭐ (Missing Step)\n\nAgar constructor khud explicitly koi object return nahi karta,\n\nto JavaScript automatically\n\nthis\n\nko return kar deta hai.\n\nInternally aisa hota hai\n\nreturn this;\n\nYe JavaScript khud karta hai.\n\n✅ Step 9: Returned Object Variable Mein Store Hota Hai\n\nAb\n\nlet s1 = new Student(\"Amar\",21);\n\nke andar\n\nreturn hua object\n\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}\n\ns1 variable ke andar store ho jata hai.\n\ns1\n |\n ▼\n{\n   name:\"Amar\",\n   age:21\n}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
