      "seed": 1410307405,
      "version": 352,
      "versionNonce": 2116657507,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785423934227,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 1. Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nConstructor ek special method hota hai jo class ke andar define kiya jata hai aur jab bhi new keyword se object create hota hai, ye\nautomatically execute ho jata hai.\n\nIska primary purpose naye object ko initialize karna hota hai. Initialization ka matlab hai object ki initial state set karna, uski properties ko\nvalues dena aur object ko use karne ke liye ready banana.\n\nConstructor ki wajah se hume object create hone ke baad baar-baar manually properties assign nahi karni padti. Har naya object ek hi process\nfollow karta hai, jisse code reusable, clean aur maintainable ban jata hai.\n\nEk class me sirf ek constructor ho sakta hai aur uska naam hamesha constructor hi hota hai.\n\nConstructor object creation lifecycle ka pehla step hota hai aur object banne ke turant baad execute hota hai.\n\n🟢 2. Default Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nDefault Constructor wo constructor hota hai jo JavaScript khud automatically provide karti hai, agar programmer ne class ke andar koi\nconstructor define nahi kiya ho.\n\nIska kaam sirf object creation process ko complete karna hota hai. Ye koi custom initialization nahi karta.\n\nAgar developer apna constructor likh deta hai, to JavaScript ka default constructor replace ho jata hai aur uske baad sirf developer wala\nconstructor hi execute hota hai.\n\nInheritance me default constructor internally parent constructor ko bhi call karta hai taaki object sahi tarike se initialize ho sake.\n\nDefault constructor ka existence isliye hai taaki har class ke paas object create karne ka mechanism ho, chahe developer ne constructor\nlikha ho ya nahi.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 1. Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nConstructor ek special method hota hai jo class ke andar define kiya jata hai aur jab bhi new keyword se object create hota hai, ye automatically execute ho jata hai.\n\nIska primary purpose naye object ko initialize karna hota hai. Initialization ka matlab hai object ki initial state set karna, uski properties ko values dena aur object ko use karne ke liye ready banana.\n\nConstructor ki wajah se hume object create hone ke baad baar-baar manually properties assign nahi karni padti. Har naya object ek hi process follow karta hai, jisse code reusable, clean aur maintainable ban jata hai.\n\nEk class me sirf ek constructor ho sakta hai aur uska naam hamesha constructor hi hota hai.\n\nConstructor object creation lifecycle ka pehla step hota hai aur object banne ke turant baad execute hota hai.\n\n🟢 2. Default Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nDefault Constructor wo constructor hota hai jo JavaScript khud automatically provide karti hai, agar programmer ne class ke andar koi constructor define nahi kiya ho.\n\nIska kaam sirf object creation process ko complete karna hota hai. Ye koi custom initialization nahi karta.\n\nAgar developer apna constructor likh deta hai, to JavaScript ka default constructor replace ho jata hai aur uske baad sirf developer wala constructor hi execute hota hai.\n\nInheritance me default constructor internally parent constructor ko bhi call karta hai taaki object sahi tarike se initialize ho sake.\n\nDefault constructor ka existence isliye hai taaki har class ke paas object create karne ka mechanism ho, chahe developer ne constructor likha ho ya nahi.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7to3Vm301Kx8ShR_BqzHN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43010.74112399101,
      "y": -3397.4680747844423,
      "width": 1648.3388671875,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4dabf7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHo",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1013887277,
      "version": 107,
      "versionNonce": 121304557,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785424220935,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 3. Parameterized Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nParameterized Constructor wo constructor hota hai jo parameters accept karta hai.\n\nIska purpose har naye object ko alag-alag values ke saath initialize karna hota hai.\n\nAgar har object ki information different hai, jaise name, age, salary ya product price, to un values ko constructor ke parameters ke through pass kiya jata hai.\n\nIsse ek hi class se multiple objects create kiye ja sakte hain jinki properties alag-alag hoti hain.\n\nParameterized constructor flexibility provide karta hai kyunki object creation ke time hi required data receive kar leta hai aur object ko usi hisaab se initialize karta hai.\n\nYe OOP ka sabse commonly used constructor type hai.\n\n🟢 4. Constructor Chaining (super()) ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nConstructor Chaining ka matlab hai ek constructor ka dusre constructor ko call karna.\n\nJavaScript me ye concept inheritance ke andar use hota hai.\n\nJab child class parent class se inherit karti hai, to parent class ki properties aur initialization ko reuse karne ke liye child constructor se super() call kiya jata hai.\n\nsuper() parent class ke constructor ko invoke karta hai.\n\nIsse parent class apni initialization complete karti hai aur uske baad child class apni additional initialization karti hai.\n\nJavaScript me derived class ke constructor ke andar this use karne se pehle super() call karna mandatory hota hai.\n\nConstructor chaining code duplication ko reduce karti hai aur inheritance ko properly implement karti hai.\n\nYe Parent → Child initialization ka sequence maintain karti hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 3. Parameterized Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nParameterized Constructor wo constructor hota hai jo parameters accept karta hai.\n\nIska purpose har naye object ko alag-alag values ke saath initialize karna hota hai.\n\nAgar har object ki information different hai, jaise name, age, salary ya product price, to un values ko constructor ke parameters ke through pass kiya jata hai.\n\nIsse ek hi class se multiple objects create kiye ja sakte hain jinki properties alag-alag hoti hain.\n\nParameterized constructor flexibility provide karta hai kyunki object creation ke time hi required data receive kar leta hai aur object ko usi hisaab se initialize karta hai.\n\nYe OOP ka sabse commonly used constructor type hai.\n\n🟢 4. Constructor Chaining (super()) ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nConstructor Chaining ka matlab hai ek constructor ka dusre constructor ko call karna.\n\nJavaScript me ye concept inheritance ke andar use hota hai.\n\nJab child class parent class se inherit karti hai, to parent class ki properties aur initialization ko reuse karne ke liye child constructor se super() call kiya jata hai.\n\nsuper() parent class ke constructor ko invoke karta hai.\n\nIsse parent class apni initialization complete karti hai aur uske baad child class apni additional initialization karti hai.\n\nJavaScript me derived class ke constructor ke andar this use karne se pehle super() call karna mandatory hota hai.\n\nConstructor chaining code duplication ko reduce karti hai aur inheritance ko properly implement karti hai.\n\nYe Parent → Child initialization ka sequence maintain karti hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Of_FWvPbevCQ_C1gGy4YH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43134.45190124512,
      "y": -2473.6053251019075,
      "width": 1665.7589111328125,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 735422531,
      "version": 65,
      "versionNonce": 1524345859,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785419515591,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 6. How new Works Internally ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nnew keyword JavaScript ka ek special operator hai jo object creation process ko automate karta hai.\n\nJab new use kiya jata hai, JavaScript internally kai steps perform karti hai.\n\nSabse pehle ek naya empty object memory me create hota hai.\n\nUske baad us object ka prototype class ke prototype se connect kiya jata hai, jisse object class ke methods access kar sakta hai.\n\nPhir constructor execute hota hai aur this us naye object ko refer karta hai.\n\nConstructor object ki properties initialize karta hai.\n\nAkhir me JavaScript wahi initialized object return kar deti hai aur wo variable me store ho jata hai.\n\nYe saare steps automatically hote hain. Isi wajah se developer ko manually object banana, prototype link karna ya return likhna nahi padta.\n\nnew keyword JavaScript ke object-oriented system ka foundation hai aur constructor ke saath milkar object creation process ko simple, consistent aur reliable banata hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 6. How new Works Internally ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nnew keyword JavaScript ka ek special operator hai jo object creation process ko automate karta hai.\n\nJab new use kiya jata hai, JavaScript internally kai steps perform karti hai.\n\nSabse pehle ek naya empty object memory me create hota hai.\n\nUske baad us object ka prototype class ke prototype se connect kiya jata hai, jisse object class ke methods access kar sakta hai.\n\nPhir constructor execute hota hai aur this us naye object ko refer karta hai.\n\nConstructor object ki properties initialize karta hai.\n\nAkhir me JavaScript wahi initialized object return kar deti hai aur wo variable me store ho jata hai.\n\nYe saare steps automatically hote hain. Isi wajah se developer ko manually object banana, prototype link karna ya return likhna nahi padta.\n\nnew keyword JavaScript ke object-oriented system ka foundation hai aur constructor ke saath milkar object creation process ko simple, consistent aur reliable banata hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
