      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[this] == this is called as the refernce of the current executed obejct .\n\nthis na koi object hai  , na koi process hai  > yeh bas ek reference hai jo appke current execution object ko define karta hai .\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[this] == this is called as the refernce of the current executed obejct .\n\nthis na koi object hai  , na koi process hai  > yeh bas ek reference hai jo appke current execution object ko define karta hai .\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "R7XtEkDbA-RcyeBZrb5wV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43227.72880251884,
      "y": -1596.2359298767728,
      "width": 2082.878662109375,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#da77f2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bHw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 416750211,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1311824877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785328224353,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 Group 4: this Keyword ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nthis JavaScript ke sabse confusing concepts me se ek hai.\n\nEk line me:\n\nthis ek variable nahi hai. this ek special keyword hai jo current execution ke context (owner object) ko refer karta hai.\n\nJavaScript me this function define hone ke time decide nahi hota, balki function call hone ke time decide hota hai (except Arrow Functions).\n\n🟢 1. this inside Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nJab hum new keyword se object create karte hain, JavaScript sabse pehle memory me ek naya empty object banati hai. Uske baad constructor execute hone se pehle this ko us naye object se bind kar diya jata hai.\n\nIsliye constructor ke andar this hamesha newly created object ko refer karta hai.\n\nConstructor ka kaam us object ko initialize karna hota hai aur this us object ke andar values store karne ka medium hota hai.\n\nAgar this na ho, to constructor ko pata hi nahi chalega ki values kis object me store karni hain.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nConstructor ke andar this ka matlab hota hai \"jo object abhi-abhi create hua hai.\"",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 Group 4: this Keyword ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nthis JavaScript ke sabse confusing concepts me se ek hai.\n\nEk line me:\n\nthis ek variable nahi hai. this ek special keyword hai jo current execution ke context (owner object) ko refer karta hai.\n\nJavaScript me this function define hone ke time decide nahi hota, balki function call hone ke time decide hota hai (except Arrow Functions).\n\n🟢 1. this inside Constructor ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nJab hum new keyword se object create karte hain, JavaScript sabse pehle memory me ek naya empty object banati hai. Uske baad constructor execute hone se pehle this ko us naye object se bind kar diya jata hai.\n\nIsliye constructor ke andar this hamesha newly created object ko refer karta hai.\n\nConstructor ka kaam us object ko initialize karna hota hai aur this us object ke andar values store karne ka medium hota hai.\n\nAgar this na ho, to constructor ko pata hi nahi chalega ki values kis object me store karni hain.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nConstructor ke andar this ka matlab hota hai \"jo object abhi-abhi create hua hai.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
