      "updated": 1785332267611,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 2. this inside Methods ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nClass ya object ke methods ke andar this us object ko refer karta hai jis object ne method ko call kiya hai.\n\nMethod kisi ek object ka permanently nahi hota.\n\nEk hi method alag-alag objects ke saath use ho sakta hai.\n\nIsliye JavaScript call ke time dekhti hai ki method kis object ke through invoke hua hai.\n\nUsi object ko this bana diya jata hai.\n\nIsi wajah se ek hi method multiple objects ke saath reuse ho sakta hai.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nMethod ke andar this = Method ko call karne wala object.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 2. this inside Methods ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\nTheory\n\nClass ya object ke methods ke andar this us object ko refer karta hai jis object ne method ko call kiya hai.\n\nMethod kisi ek object ka permanently nahi hota.\n\nEk hi method alag-alag objects ke saath use ho sakta hai.\n\nIsliye JavaScript call ke time dekhti hai ki method kis object ke through invoke hua hai.\n\nUsi object ko this bana diya jata hai.\n\nIsi wajah se ek hi method multiple objects ke saath reuse ho sakta hai.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nMethod ke andar this = Method ko call karne wala object.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
