    {
      "id": "Y1K6ymH9VuiMDrH2r6LGR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43426.918127665966,
      "y": 1151.7212188477838,
      "width": 1545.1392822265625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bI9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1557835779,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 1725490403,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785425125479,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟢 5. Losing this ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐     \nTheory\n\n\"Losing this\" ka matlab hai ki function apne original object se alag hokar execute ho gaya aur JavaScript ko pata hi nahi chala ki this kis object ko refer kare.\n\nYe tab hota hai jab object ka method alag nikal kar call kiya jata hai, callback me pass kar diya jata hai, ya kisi aur jagah execute ho jata hai.\n\nKyunki Normal Function ka this call ke time decide hota hai, agar object ka reference lose ho gaya to this bhi change ho jayega.\n\nIsi problem ko Losing this bolte hain.\n\nYe JavaScript ka bug nahi hai, balki uska design hai.\n\nIs problem ko solve karne ke common ways:\n\nbind()\nArrow Function\ncall()\napply()\nWrapper Function\n\nSimple words me:\n\nMethod object se alag hua → Object ka connection toot gaya → this bhi lose ho gaya.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟢 5. Losing this ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐     \nTheory\n\n\"Losing this\" ka matlab hai ki function apne original object se alag hokar execute ho gaya aur JavaScript ko pata hi nahi chala ki this kis object ko refer kare.\n\nYe tab hota hai jab object ka method alag nikal kar call kiya jata hai, callback me pass kar diya jata hai, ya kisi aur jagah execute ho jata hai.\n\nKyunki Normal Function ka this call ke time decide hota hai, agar object ka reference lose ho gaya to this bhi change ho jayega.\n\nIsi problem ko Losing this bolte hain.\n\nYe JavaScript ka bug nahi hai, balki uska design hai.\n\nIs problem ko solve karne ke common ways:\n\nbind()\nArrow Function\ncall()\napply()\nWrapper Function\n\nSimple words me:\n\nMethod object se alag hua → Object ka connection toot gaya → this bhi lose ho gaya.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YXUVlneIwVQMdEuWQhT7B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43421.36270774409,
      "y": 1968.3879363770807,
      "width": 291.71978759765625,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 849856301,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 353869805,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785335137971,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "const person = {\n    name: \"Amar\",\n\n    greet() {\n        console.log(this.name);\n    }\n};\n\nconst sayHello = person.greet;\n\nsayHello();",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "const person = {\n    name: \"Amar\",\n\n    greet() {\n        console.log(this.name);\n    }\n};\n\nconst sayHello = person.greet;\n\nsayHello();",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Y1yjN1XvivxEdfJB1LeCx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 43443.58469260737,
      "y": 2407.276638769659,
      "width": 2302.1982421875,
      "height": 1625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e64980",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1652050093,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 282444141,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785335213071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bilkul. Isko bas 3 points me yaad rakhna.\n\n⭐ Losing this ka Reason (Minimal)\nReason 1\n\nJavaScript me this function ke saath permanently attach nahi hota.\n\nReason 2\n\nJab function call hota hai, JavaScript sirf ek cheez dekhti hai:\n\n\"Is function ko kis object ne call kiya?\"\n\nUsi object ko this bana deti hai.\n\nReason 3\n\nAgar method object se alag ho jaye,\n\nconst hello = person.greet;\n\nhello();\n\nto JavaScript ko koi owner object nahi milta.\n\nIsliye\n\nthis = undefined\n\n(strict mode)\n\nEasy Flow\nperson.greet()\n\n↓\n\nOwner = person\n\n↓\n\nthis = person ✅\n\nBut\n\nconst hello = person.greet;\n\n↓\n\nhello()\n\n↓\n\nOwner = ❌\n\n↓\n\nthis = undefined ❌\nInterview Line ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nLosing this happens because JavaScript determines this at function call time. If a method is called without its original object, JavaScript cannot find the owner object, so this loses its reference and becomes undefined (in strict mode).\n\nYaad rakhne ka Formula\n\nNo Owner = No this ❌\nOwner Present = Correct this ✅",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bilkul. Isko bas 3 points me yaad rakhna.\n\n⭐ Losing this ka Reason (Minimal)\nReason 1\n\nJavaScript me this function ke saath permanently attach nahi hota.\n\nReason 2\n\nJab function call hota hai, JavaScript sirf ek cheez dekhti hai:\n\n\"Is function ko kis object ne call kiya?\"\n\nUsi object ko this bana deti hai.\n\nReason 3\n\nAgar method object se alag ho jaye,\n\nconst hello = person.greet;\n\nhello();\n\nto JavaScript ko koi owner object nahi milta.\n\nIsliye\n\nthis = undefined\n\n(strict mode)\n\nEasy Flow\nperson.greet()\n\n↓\n\nOwner = person\n\n↓\n\nthis = person ✅\n\nBut\n\nconst hello = person.greet;\n\n↓\n\nhello()\n\n↓\n\nOwner = ❌\n\n↓\n\nthis = undefined ❌\nInterview Line ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nLosing this happens because JavaScript determines this at function call time. If a method is called without its original object, JavaScript cannot find the owner object, so this loses its reference and becomes undefined (in strict mode).\n\nYaad rakhne ka Formula\n\nNo Owner = No this ❌\nOwner Present = Correct this ✅",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
