    {
      "id": "OA1-bzGxI7HHOEkg6NeNE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 53550.603218967444,
      "y": -6891.154598414428,
      "width": 1914.8408406575545,
      "height": 1645,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 828118059,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 428793125,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785574969758,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Encapsulation (Hinglish)\n\n**Encapsulation** OOP ka ek principle hai jo **properties (data) aur methods (functions) ko ek single unit (Class) ke andar wrap/bind\nkarta hai.** Iska main purpose data ko protect karna aur uske access ko control karna hota hai.\n\n## Encapsulation use kyu karte hain?\n\n### 1. Direct Access ko rokne ke liye (Data Hiding)\n\nBy default, object ki properties **public** hoti hain, yani koi bhi outside code unhe directly access ya modify kar sakta hai.\n\nIs problem ko solve karne ke liye hum properties ko **private (`#`)** bana dete hain.\n\nAb outside code unhe directly access nahi kar sakta. Agar access ya update karna ho to **Getter** aur **Setter** ke through hi hoga.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Data Hiding\n\nData Hiding ka matlab hai object ka internal data bahar se hide rahe.\n\nIsse koi bhi user accidentally ya intentionally data ko direct change nahi kar sakta.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Code ko Organized banana\n\nProperties aur unse related methods ek hi class ke andar rehte hain.\n\nIsse code clean, readable aur maintain karna easy ho jata hai.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Code Reusability\n\nEk baar class bana do, fir usse jitne chahe objects bana sakte ho.\n\nHar baar same properties aur methods dobara likhne ki zarurat nahi padti.\n\n---\n\n## Interview Definition\n\n**Encapsulation ek OOP principle hai jo properties aur methods ko ek single unit (Class) ke andar bind karta hai aur private fields ke\nthrough direct access ko restrict karta hai. Data ko access ya update karne ke liye Getter aur Setter use kiye jate hain. Isse data\nsecure rehta hai aur code clean aur maintainable banta hai.**\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Encapsulation (Hinglish)\n\n**Encapsulation** OOP ka ek principle hai jo **properties (data) aur methods (functions) ko ek single unit (Class) ke andar wrap/bind karta hai.** Iska main purpose data ko protect karna aur uske access ko control karna hota hai.\n\n## Encapsulation use kyu karte hain?\n\n### 1. Direct Access ko rokne ke liye (Data Hiding)\n\nBy default, object ki properties **public** hoti hain, yani koi bhi outside code unhe directly access ya modify kar sakta hai.\n\nIs problem ko solve karne ke liye hum properties ko **private (`#`)** bana dete hain.\n\nAb outside code unhe directly access nahi kar sakta. Agar access ya update karna ho to **Getter** aur **Setter** ke through hi hoga.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Data Hiding\n\nData Hiding ka matlab hai object ka internal data bahar se hide rahe.\n\nIsse koi bhi user accidentally ya intentionally data ko direct change nahi kar sakta.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Code ko Organized banana\n\nProperties aur unse related methods ek hi class ke andar rehte hain.\n\nIsse code clean, readable aur maintain karna easy ho jata hai.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Code Reusability\n\nEk baar class bana do, fir usse jitne chahe objects bana sakte ho.\n\nHar baar same properties aur methods dobara likhne ki zarurat nahi padti.\n\n---\n\n## Interview Definition\n\n**Encapsulation ek OOP principle hai jo properties aur methods ko ek single unit (Class) ke andar bind karta hai aur private fields ke through direct access ko restrict karta hai. Data ko access ya update karne ke liye Getter aur Setter use kiye jate hain. Isse data secure rehta hai aur code clean aur maintainable banta hai.**\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
