    {
      "id": "CiFi4hx8r4GobK_5HgPbs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 53384.21316381995,
      "y": -442.8332625880257,
      "width": 2961.7634887695312,
      "height": 2030,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 865019787,
      "version": 39,
      "versionNonce": 1013199429,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785575992860,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Private Members (`#`) - Real Data Hiding\n\nJavaScript mein pehle **private members** ka concept built-in nahi tha. Isliye developers **Closures** ka use karke data hide (encapsulate) karte the.\n\nES2022 ke baad JavaScript ne **Private Fields (`#`)** introduce kiye, jisse **real/official data hiding** possible hui.\n\n## Closure vs Private Members\n\n### Before ES2022 (Closures)\n\n* Private variables closure ke through banaye jate the.\n* Data lexical environment mein store hota tha.\n* Ye ek programming technique thi, language feature nahi.\n\n### After ES2022 (`#` Private Members)\n\n* JavaScript language ne officially private members provide kiye.\n* `#variable` ko class ke bahar se access ya modify nahi kar sakte.\n* Agar bahar se access karne ki koshish karoge to error milega.\n* Sirf class ke andar ke methods hi `#` members ko access kar sakte hain.\n\n## Example\n\n```javascript\nclass Person {\n  #name;\n\n  constructor(name) {\n    this.#name = name;\n  }\n\n  getName() {\n    return this.#name;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nYahan `#name` completely private hai.\n\n```javascript\nconst p = new Person(\"Amar\");\n\nconsole.log(p.#name); // ❌ Error\n```\n\nDirect access allowed nahi hai.\n\nSirf:\n\n```javascript\nconsole.log(p.getName()); // ✅ Amar\n```\n\n## Interview Definition\n\n**Private Members (`#`) JavaScript ka built-in feature hai jo real data hiding provide karta hai. Ye class ke private data ko outside code se protect karta hai. Private members ko sirf class ke andar hi access ya\nmodify kiya ja sakta hai. Ye Closures ki tarah ek workaround nahi, balki JavaScript language ka official feature hai.**\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Private Members (`#`) - Real Data Hiding\n\nJavaScript mein pehle **private members** ka concept built-in nahi tha. Isliye developers **Closures** ka use karke data hide (encapsulate) karte the.\n\nES2022 ke baad JavaScript ne **Private Fields (`#`)** introduce kiye, jisse **real/official data hiding** possible hui.\n\n## Closure vs Private Members\n\n### Before ES2022 (Closures)\n\n* Private variables closure ke through banaye jate the.\n* Data lexical environment mein store hota tha.\n* Ye ek programming technique thi, language feature nahi.\n\n### After ES2022 (`#` Private Members)\n\n* JavaScript language ne officially private members provide kiye.\n* `#variable` ko class ke bahar se access ya modify nahi kar sakte.\n* Agar bahar se access karne ki koshish karoge to error milega.\n* Sirf class ke andar ke methods hi `#` members ko access kar sakte hain.\n\n## Example\n\n```javascript\nclass Person {\n  #name;\n\n  constructor(name) {\n    this.#name = name;\n  }\n\n  getName() {\n    return this.#name;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nYahan `#name` completely private hai.\n\n```javascript\nconst p = new Person(\"Amar\");\n\nconsole.log(p.#name); // ❌ Error\n```\n\nDirect access allowed nahi hai.\n\nSirf:\n\n```javascript\nconsole.log(p.getName()); // ✅ Amar\n```\n\n## Interview Definition\n\n**Private Members (`#`) JavaScript ka built-in feature hai jo real data hiding provide karta hai. Ye class ke private data ko outside code se protect karta hai. Private members ko sirf class ke andar hi access ya modify kiya ja sakta hai. Ye Closures ki tarah ek workaround nahi, balki JavaScript language ka official feature hai.**\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
