      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## `extends`\n\n* `extends` JavaScript ka ek **keyword** hai.\n\n* Ye **child class ko parent class se inherit** karwata hai.\n\n* Iski wajah se child class ko **parent ki properties aur methods** mil jaati hain.\n\n* `extends` ke baad hi child class ke andar `super()` use kar sakte hain.\n\n* `extends` sirf constructor ke liye nahi hota, balki **poori class ko inherit** karta hai.\n\n* JavaScript me `extends` **class expressions** ke saath bhi use ho sakta hai, sirf class declarations ke saath hi nahi.\n\n### Easy Definition\n\n**`extends` parent aur child class ke beech relationship banata hai. Iski wajah se child class parent ki saari non-private properties aur methods inherit kar leti hai. Isi relationship ki wajah se `super()` kaam karta hai.**\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## `extends`\n\n* `extends` JavaScript ka ek **keyword** hai.\n\n* Ye **child class ko parent class se inherit** karwata hai.\n\n* Iski wajah se child class ko **parent ki properties aur methods** mil jaati hain.\n\n* `extends` ke baad hi child class ke andar `super()` use kar sakte hain.\n\n* `extends` sirf constructor ke liye nahi hota, balki **poori class ko inherit** karta hai.\n\n* JavaScript me `extends` **class expressions** ke saath bhi use ho sakta hai, sirf class declarations ke saath hi nahi.\n\n### Easy Definition\n\n**`extends` parent aur child class ke beech relationship banata hai. Iski wajah se child class parent ki saari non-private properties aur methods inherit kar leti hai. Isi relationship ki wajah se `super()` kaam karta hai.**\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
