      "locked": false,
      "text": "        Parent Class\n      (Common Features)\n             │\n          extends\n             │\n        Child Class\n (Inherited + Own Features)",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "        Parent Class\n      (Common Features)\n             │\n          extends\n             │\n        Child Class\n (Inherited + Own Features)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gkpkVfq_bJszvy4Cvwz5I",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58288.19832909812,
      "y": -2402.288778274411,
      "width": 3029.6735839843736,
      "height": 814.4836694089029,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 743518123,
      "version": 90,
      "versionNonce": 1977067813,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785594864585,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Jab Child Class, Parent Class ke kisi method ko same name aur same parameters ke saath dobara define karti hai, to usse Method Overriding kehte hain.\n\nPurpose:\n\nParent ke default behavior ko customize karna.\nChild Class ke according alag implementation dena.\nRuntime Polymorphism achieve karna.\n\nImportant Points:\n\nMethod ka name same hona chahiye.\nMethod ke parameters same hone chahiye.\nChild Class Parent Class ko extends karti hai.\nChild object se method call karne par Child ka method execute hota hai.\nParent ka method delete ya replace nahi hota, balki Child ke liye override (hide) ho jata hai.\nAgar Parent ka method bhi use karna ho, to super keyword ka use kiya ja sakta hai.",
      "fontSize": 40.72418347044516,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Jab Child Class, Parent Class ke kisi method ko same name aur same parameters ke saath dobara define karti hai, to usse Method Overriding kehte hain.\n\nPurpose:\n\nParent ke default behavior ko customize karna.\nChild Class ke according alag implementation dena.\nRuntime Polymorphism achieve karna.\n\nImportant Points:\n\nMethod ka name same hona chahiye.\nMethod ke parameters same hone chahiye.\nChild Class Parent Class ko extends karti hai.\nChild object se method call karne par Child ka method execute hota hai.\nParent ka method delete ya replace nahi hota, balki Child ke liye override (hide) ho jata hai.\nAgar Parent ka method bhi use karna ho, to super keyword ka use kiya ja sakta hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
