    {
      "id": "Rca1ZJCUViGEKNRdetVTQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 63237.233627020556,
      "y": -3578.546908954577,
      "width": 3488.517822265625,
      "height": 2240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bOC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1477818725,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 766915115,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785667303557,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How JavaScript Simulates Abstract Classes\n\nJavaScript mein hum normally 2 techniques use karte hain.\n\n1. Constructor Check (Object banne se rokna)\nclass Vehicle {\n    constructor() {\n        if (new.target === Vehicle) {\n            throw new Error(\"Cannot create object of Abstract Class\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nYahan kya ho raha hai?\n\nAgar koi kare:\nnew Vehicle();\n\nTo error aa jayega.\n\nMatlab JS ne abstract class jaisa behavior create kar diya.\n\n2. Abstract Method Simulate Karna\nclass Vehicle {\n    start() {\n        throw new Error(\"start() must be implemented\");\n    }\n}\n\nAb agar child class start() ko override nahi karegi:\n\nclass Car extends Vehicle {}\n\nconst c = new Car();\nc.start();\n\nOutput:\n\nError: start() must be implemented\n\nMatlab developer ko force kiya ja raha hai ki method implement karo.\n\nFlow\nVehicle (Base Class)\n        │\n        ├── new Vehicle() ❌\n        │      throw Error\n        │\n        └── start()\n               │\n               └── throw Error\n\n        ↓\n\nCar extends Vehicle\n        │\n        └── start() override karega ✔\nInterview Answer ⭐\n\nJavaScript does not support abstract classes natively because it has no abstract keyword. We simulate abstract classes by preventing direct object creation using new.target and by throwing errors in methods that child classes are expected to override.\n\nYaad rakhne ki trick\nJava → abstract keyword built-in hai.\nJavaScript → abstract keyword nahi hai, isliye new.target + throw new Error() se abstract class jaisa behavior simulate karte hain.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How JavaScript Simulates Abstract Classes\n\nJavaScript mein hum normally 2 techniques use karte hain.\n\n1. Constructor Check (Object banne se rokna)\nclass Vehicle {\n    constructor() {\n        if (new.target === Vehicle) {\n            throw new Error(\"Cannot create object of Abstract Class\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nYahan kya ho raha hai?\n\nAgar koi kare:\nnew Vehicle();\n\nTo error aa jayega.\n\nMatlab JS ne abstract class jaisa behavior create kar diya.\n\n2. Abstract Method Simulate Karna\nclass Vehicle {\n    start() {\n        throw new Error(\"start() must be implemented\");\n    }\n}\n\nAb agar child class start() ko override nahi karegi:\n\nclass Car extends Vehicle {}\n\nconst c = new Car();\nc.start();\n\nOutput:\n\nError: start() must be implemented\n\nMatlab developer ko force kiya ja raha hai ki method implement karo.\n\nFlow\nVehicle (Base Class)\n        │\n        ├── new Vehicle() ❌\n        │      throw Error\n        │\n        └── start()\n               │\n               └── throw Error\n\n        ↓\n\nCar extends Vehicle\n        │\n        └── start() override karega ✔\nInterview Answer ⭐\n\nJavaScript does not support abstract classes natively because it has no abstract keyword. We simulate abstract classes by preventing direct object creation using new.target and by throwing errors in methods that child classes are expected to override.\n\nYaad rakhne ki trick\nJava → abstract keyword built-in hai.\nJavaScript → abstract keyword nahi hai, isliye new.target + throw new Error() se abstract class jaisa behavior simulate karte hain.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
